      "visionTurn": {
        "answer": "U.S. agricultural exports shifted markedly toward the Americas and developing East Asia between 1995–99 and 2011–15. Developing East Asia rose from 8% to 23% and North America from 22% to 28%, while high-income Asia-Pacific fell from 33% to 20% and Europe and Central Asia from 20% to 11%; other regions remained relatively small and mostly stable.",
